dragonfixes.research_page.witchwood_rod=Your studies into other schools of magic have led you to discover an unusual tree known as Witchwood. Unlike Silverwood, which has a natural affinity for Vis, Witchwood appears to be particularly receptive to mana. Feeling experimental, you attempted to infuse it with purified Vinteum dust.<BR><BR>Your first results were catastrophic, but after reinforcing the rod with some Ent twigs, you have managed to create a rod capable of converting mana into Vis.<BR><BR>And it paid off! The resulting wand can store %d vis of each primal aspect. On top of that, it gradually replenishes its reserves by drawing upon your mana! Unfortunately, it is not very efficient: it costs 140 mana per point of vis.<BR><BR>Further research may reveal ways to improve its efficiency...
dragonfixes.research_page.witchwood_staff=Although your experiments with Witchwood have proven successful, the wand's rather slow recharge rate makes it impractical for prolonged magical endeavors.<BR><BR>Unfortunately, Witchwood seems to react poorly to elemental crystals, making the creation of a conventional staff considerably more difficult. After some experimentation, you've managed to overcome this problem, albeit at the expense of its storage capacity.<BR><BR>While the resulting staff can only store %d vis of each primal aspect, it replenishes its reserves two and a half times as quickly as its smaller counterpart, consuming only 100 mana per point of vis.<BR><BR>Perhaps sacrificing storage capacity wasn't such a bad idea after all...
dragonfixes.research_page.vinteum_cap=Further experimentation with Witchwood has led you to suspect that some of the mana drawn by the rod is lost during its conversion into Vis. Given the role Vinteum played in your original experiments, you wondered whether it could also help reduce these losses.<BR><BR>Since Vinteum is merely a more ordered form of Thaumium, you cannot expect it to offer a greater Vis discount. However, its ordered nature allows you to harness its magical properties without the need for infusion.<BR><BR>Much to your delight, fitting a Witchwood wand with these caps reduces its mana consumption to just 80 mana per point of vis. When used with a Witchwood staff, this cost is further reduced to 50 mana.<BR><BR>Now that's a considerable improvement!
